---
title: Kamal Power Laundry - Authentication and Supplier Purchase Sequence
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Owner
    participant UI as Browser UI
    participant API as Express API
    participant Auth as Supabase Auth
    participant DB as Supabase PostgreSQL

    Owner->>UI: Enter username and password
    UI->>API: POST /api/login
    API->>Auth: signInWithPassword(email, password)
    alt Credentials invalid
        Auth-->>API: Authentication error
        API-->>UI: 401 Incorrect username or password
        UI-->>Owner: Show login error
    else Credentials valid
        Auth-->>API: Authenticated user ID and email
        API-->>UI: Create session and return username
        UI->>API: GET /api/state
        API->>DB: Ensure public.users profile exists
        DB-->>API: User profile ready
        API->>DB: Load customers, services, orders, items, inventory
        DB-->>API: Application data
        API-->>UI: Return dashboard data
        UI-->>Owner: Show shop desk
    end

    opt Create supplier purchase
        Owner->>UI: Enter supplier, date, items, quantities, costs, and payment
        UI->>UI: Calculate totals, payment status, and balance
        UI->>API: POST /api/purchases
        API->>DB: Validate and execute create_purchase RPC
        DB->>DB: Insert purchase and purchase items atomically
        DB-->>API: Purchase ID
        API->>DB: Load saved purchase
        DB-->>API: Purchase data
        API-->>UI: 201 Created
        UI-->>Owner: Show purchase details and status
    end

    opt Update supplier payment
        Owner->>UI: Choose payment status or enter amount paid
        UI->>UI: Preview derived payment status and balance
        UI->>API: PATCH /api/purchases/{id}/payment
        API->>DB: Update amount_paid, balance_amount, payment_status
        DB-->>API: Updated purchase
        API-->>UI: Updated payment details
        UI-->>Owner: Refresh PAYMENT badge and balance
    end

    opt Change purchase status to Received
        Owner->>UI: Confirm receipt
        UI->>API: POST /api/purchases/{id}/receive
        API->>DB: Execute receive_purchase RPC
        DB->>DB: Lock purchase and validate Draft or Ordered
        loop Each purchase item
            DB->>DB: Create inventory item if needed
            DB->>DB: Increase stock and update inventory timestamps
            DB->>DB: Insert PURCHASE stock transaction
        end
        DB->>DB: Set purchase status to Received
        DB-->>API: Receipt result
        API-->>UI: Purchase received
        UI-->>Owner: Refresh status and inventory
    end

    opt Change purchase status to Draft, Ordered, or Cancelled
        Owner->>UI: Choose status and confirm cancellation when selected
        UI->>API: PUT /api/purchases/{id} or DELETE /api/purchases/{id}
        API->>DB: Validate and update purchase status
        API->>DB: Cancellation is pre-receipt only and stock remains unchanged
        DB-->>API: Updated purchase
        API-->>UI: Updated status
        UI-->>Owner: Refresh STATUS badge
    end
